  "verbalization": "Michaolide E is shown to have a target relationship with Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 5-(2-Thienylethynyl)-2-thiophenemethanol. All these compounds share a common target of SF-188, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The evidence supports a pathway where Michaolide E may interact with Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, potentially influencing its activity and leading to the activation of SF-188. The presence of multiple compounds with similar targets reinforces the idea that SF-188 may be a downstream effector of these interactions, though the exact mechanism of how Michaolide E influences Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like remains to be fully elucidated.",
